From 76f67cbb9bdd822918e44520d8c66fa3e8908499 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:01:49 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sim): generate a loose machine model posed by axis
 values

Add `camcraft_sim::machine_model`. Its input is plain data of its own
(parts, parent, joint kind, axis, travel, spindle body, tool station),
so `camcraft-sim` gets no edge to `camcraft-post`.

- One closed body for each part that states a number: a block for a
  table or a slide, a cylinder for the spindle body, and the tool
  envelope of the tool station as a body of its own kind.
- `MachineModel::pose` moves the bodies along the joint chain (linear
  and rotary joints, pivot and offset) for a set of axis values.
- Each body is marked `BodySource::Generated`; a check reports
  "judged on a generated model".
- A part with no number gets no body and a named note.
- Degenerate input and a bad pose refuse by the part id and the key.

Fixes #2584

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
